    "image": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504450758481-7338eba7524a?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3wyNjI5NjF8MHwxfHNlYXJjaHwyfHxCYXNrZXRiYWxsJTIwQXJlbmF8ZW58MHx8fHwxNjkzODc4NTA1fDA&ixlib=rb-4.0.3&q=80&w=1080",
    "category": "Archive",
    "content": "<p>Don’t focus on the haters; not those who call out every misstep or point out how things could’ve gone better. Give props to the one who’s really in the game, grinding it out with sweat, grit, and heart; who keeps pushing forward; who messes up and falls short time after time, because nothing worth doing comes without its setbacks; but who still fights to make things happen; who feels that fire and passion; who gives their all for something that matters; who, at their best, knows the sweet taste of success, and who, at their worst, fails with courage, never settling among the cautious and hesitant folks who don’t know what it’s like to win or lose. – Teddy Roosevelt, Remix</p>"
